WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.168 --> 00:00:02.211
- Our flight has gone down.

00:00:02.211 --> 00:00:03.837
This is an emergency.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.507
- [Narrator] Survive
together or die alone.

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:08.300
- We're getting off this island.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.844
(radio crackling)

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.388
(airplane roaring)
(dramatic music)

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:15.057
- Captain Torrance,
flight commander.

00:00:15.057 --> 00:00:16.141
How can I help you?

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:16.975
- Fugitive extradition.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.603
- Well, is he dangerous?

00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:20.646
What did he do?

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:22.189
- Homicide, 15 years ago.

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:23.357
- [Torrance] I
don't want to scare

00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:25.067
the rest of the passengers.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.777
- [Man] I'm afraid you're
stuck with us, Captain.

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:28.195
- Get 'em on board,
let's have a good flight.

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:31.406
(dramatic music intensifies)
(thunder roars)

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:34.034
Cutting right through
the top of the storm.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.577
(bell dings)

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:36.703
Listen, keep everybody
in their seats.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.163
No exceptions, all right?

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:39.790
(plane rumbling)
- I need everyone

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.917
to have their seatbelts
securely fastened!

00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:45.754
(dramatic music continues)

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.048
- Mayday, mayday, mayday.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.843
Blazer 119, we are dark.
(console beeping)

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:52.553
Does anyone hear us, goddamn it?

00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:54.221
- We're gonna hit,
we're gonna hit!

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:58.350
(dramatic music)
(plane roaring)

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.227
(suspenseful music)

00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:02.813
- They went down somewhere
in the Jolo Island cluster.

00:01:04.106 --> 00:01:05.816
It's run by separatists
and militias.

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:07.609
The Filipino army won't
even go there anymore.

00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:11.822
The clock is ticking.
Every minute matters.

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:14.366
(clock ticks)

00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:16.952
We can count those minutes
in lives lost or saved.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.371
(people shouting)
- Guys, wait, wait.

00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:21.206
Get back, we don't
know who it is.

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:22.708
We don't know who
it is, get back!

00:01:22.708 --> 00:01:23.876
- Listen carefully.

00:01:23.876 --> 00:01:25.210
This is an emergency.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.337
I'm Captain Brodie Torrance.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:33.468
(gun fires)
(dramatic music)

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:35.262
- I like this guy.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:40.350
- Name, country!
- Maxwell Carver, England.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.685
- Name, country.

00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:46.648
(gun fires)
(people screaming)

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:48.233
- I gotta go after them.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:51.528
They're my passengers,
my responsibility.

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:53.197
I'm gonna need your help.

00:01:53.197 --> 00:01:55.741
- You're gonna need this.

00:01:55.741 --> 00:01:57.367
- Former military or something?

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.535
- [Louis] You could say that.

00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:01.788
- [Torrance] Why'd
they lock you up?

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.415
- No one cares what
really happened.

00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:04.958
But they say
redemption can be found

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.085
in the most unusual places.

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:09.922
(body thudding)
(dramatic music)

00:02:09.922 --> 00:02:12.883
If you do this, you'll probably
never see your family again.

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:14.218
- What about their families?

00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:18.555
I have a daughter and
I have every intention

00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:19.431
of making it home.

00:02:19.431 --> 00:02:21.308
(man screams)

00:02:21.308 --> 00:02:23.644
They are gonna come at us
with everything they've got.

00:02:26.313 --> 00:02:27.523
- [Louis] We're getting
off this island.

00:02:27.523 --> 00:02:31.902
(guns firing)
(dramatic music)

00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:34.738
(radio crackling)

